h washer is shown below). \n\n![](images/9d/9d68e0672b26293e97fd8f8b2fbae4b4e3f743799d26a24291a3fd13075763d2.png)\n\nThe cross-sectional area of each washer corresponds to the region between two discs of radius ![](images/b9/b9f0db1d3432899cc481800eb60264a89a79ed6b611df8154be3fe42c37283d9.svg) and ![](images/0a/0a6417d7b72bf8af441e07e5b6ab87c0a7c6fb55520d22ab9bc175784595d811.svg) so the area of each washer cross-section is \n\n![](images/be/becabc91e909a4378a952ea7093d3e41329bf69861125d53f934bf346bbfe3f1.svg)\n\nand this is what we integrate.\n\nIn our example, the outer curve is ![](images/02/02e779dd5a005a08c5d479b17e3b9fda2f5c96f0483bba826a722f379b8c9c59.svg) and the inner curve is ![](images/34/344c03d67f3618b1dc0560c072fc86443bf8eb991de0eed6ed1196fe20586053.svg) so the volume is given by\n\n![](images/8b/8b555bb0836cb4a4a237faf7e1238332db6dbb5c9c8799e6db28b7ffb72c0cf1.svg)\n\nwhich simplifies to\n![](images/f4/f4bc30c392b233cc455162bb29c01f96c06aad15c5c6e3111cca35c32b4e6f12.svg)\n\nEvaluating this integral gives\n\n![](images/8e/8e82f449a8685fac34a3800371b4de23c09aa830fa80fe8d8140e7a618372221.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "1c7872ee-a22d-525d-8be2-58494ec5527b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1061 :tutorial/title "Rotation About the Y-Axis"} :step/id #uuid "b59996f6-161f-59af-88a3-8a99373ad18f" :step/math-academy-id 639687 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069727}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069693 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068776 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068618 :question/id #uuid "a22887cf-cafa-5ba5-9834-e0c435ec86af" :question/math-academy-id "e-592"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7144a491-71ac-565e-9687-3c8ed0a0c0a9" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069015} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069016} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529090} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529117} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529165}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Volume of a Solid Generated by Rotation About the Y-Axis"} :step/id #uuid "0fef592